# Parallel agents

Before spawning or integrating sibling Cursor agents, read [docs/AGENT_LESSONS.md](../../docs/AGENT_LESSONS.md).

- Assume siblings may write into `/workspace` even when asked to use a worktree. Do not checkout/commit there while they run unless ownership is proven disjoint.
- Give each agent a disjoint path list. Serialize edits to `CMakeLists.txt`, `tests/harness.hpp`, and `tests/unit/test_main.cpp`, or have only the parent touch them.
- Subagents often cannot `ManagePullRequest`; the parent opens PRs after push and subscribes CI.
- If the tree is interleaved: commit a WIP snapshot branch, then path-checkout onto clean `cursor/<feature>-c006` branches from the correct base. Trim CMake/docs per branch before build.
- Re-run `git status` immediately before every commit; restore unexpected paths.
